course: dictionary
lesson: 16035
title: Verified: checked and shown to be true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Verified means checked and shown to be true or correct. When you verify an answer, you test it to make sure it really works. «Sam added the numbers again, and the answer was verified.» Sam checked his work, so his answer is correct.
explain: Look at the word's family too. Verify is the base word, verifies and verifying show what someone is doing, and verified is the past form. «The teacher verified the results after the experiment.» Here verified means the teacher checked the results and found them right.
explain: Verified can also describe an online account that has been confirmed as real. «Her account is verified, so it really belongs to the singer.» A verified badge shows the account is real. It does not mean every post on it is true, so you still need to check the message itself.
fact: Verify means to check that something is true or correct.
fact: «Verified» is the past form of verify, so it describes something that has already been checked.
fact: In maths, you can verify an answer by working backwards or by checking it another way.
fact: In science, a result is often verified by repeating the experiment and getting the same answer.
fact: A verified account is confirmed as real, but a verified account can still post things that are wrong.
exercise: «Sam added the numbers again, and the answer was verified.» What does verified mean here? | Rounded up to the nearest ten | Written in pencil | Lost and never found | *Checked and shown to be correct
exercise: Maya says, «Check your answer by working backwards.» What is she asking you to do? | Change the question | Guess a new number | Draw a picture of a tree | *Verify your answer
exercise: Which word is the past form of verify? | verifying | verify | verifies | *verified
test: «The scientists repeated the experiment, and the results were independently verified.» What does verified mean? | Hidden from the public | *Checked and confirmed as correct | Changed into a new result | Thrown away
test: A blue tick shows that an account is verified. What does this tell you? | *The account has been confirmed as real | The account has no followers | Everything the account posts is true | The account is a robot
exam: «Her account is verified, but one of its posts was wrong.» What does this show? | The post was checked and proved correct | The account is fake and should be deleted | *The account is real, but its posts can still be wrong | Every post on the account must be true
